## A `MutexGuard` temporary (`m.lock!.get`) is released at the end of the
## statement that created it. Before, a guard that was never bound to a
## local was never dropped: a helper that locked deadlocked on its second
## call, and so did a second `m.lock!` in the same function.
def peek(m: &Mutex[Int]) -> Int
  m.lock!.get
end

m = Mutex.new(5)
puts peek(m)
puts peek(m)
puts m.lock!.get
puts m.lock!.get + 1
puts "no deadlock"
